      "designator": "23-0",
      "subpart_at_time": "Design and Construction",
      "title_at_amendment": "Primary flight controls.",
      "text": "(a) Primary flight controls are those used by the pilot for the immediate control of pitch, roll, and yaw. (b) The design of two-control airplanes must minimize the likelihood of complete loss of lateral or directional control in the event of failure of any connecting or transmitting element in the control system.",
